{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MobiusEnergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MobiusEnergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.PathIntegrals","lean:module:QOU.MassDerivation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":77,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.no_universal_classicalLimitConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.no_universal_classicalLimitConst","kind":"theorem","line":696,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L696-L704","doc":"**No universal constant exists** for the structure as encoded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.classicalLimitConst_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.classicalLimitConst_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":688,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L688-L694","doc":"**The constant is surjective onto ℝ** as soon as one instance exists —\nat fixed classical energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.shiftEnergy_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.shiftEnergy_const","kind":"theorem","line":685,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L685-L686","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.shiftEnergy_classicalEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.shiftEnergy_classicalEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":682,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L682-L683","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.shiftEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.shiftEnergy","kind":"def","line":671,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L671-L680","doc":"From any instance, another with the SAME classical energy and the\nconstant shifted by an arbitrary `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.classicalLimit_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.classicalLimit_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L639-L647","doc":"**So the classical-limit field relates the two energies not at all.** For\n*any* real `e` and *any* classical energy `c`, exactly one constant makes the\nequation hold. A field that can always be satisfied, whatever the quantities it\nmentions, asserts nothing about them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.classicalLimitConst_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.classicalLimitConst_eq","kind":"theorem","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L633-L637","doc":"**`classicalLimitConst` is determined by the other two fields.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.exclusionZone_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.exclusionZone_positive","kind":"theorem","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L606-L610","doc":"At `q > 1`, the exclusion zone has positive radius, providing\na genuine obstruction to self-intersection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L601-L604","doc":"The exclusion radius vanishes in the classical limit `q → 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.separation_ge_exclusionRadius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.separation_ge_exclusionRadius","kind":"theorem","line":591,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L591-L599","doc":"**The exclusion, derived rather than assumed.**  No two strand points of\nan inhabitant come within the exclusion radius: if one pair did, the\nbarrier field would make the energy exceed itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.exclusionRadius_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.exclusionRadius_pos","kind":"theorem","line":581,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L581-L589","doc":"The exclusion radius is positive — **derived** from `cme.q_gt_one`\nthrough `hbarQ_pos`, not carried.  It was a structure field\n(`exclusionRadius_pos`) until 2026-08-30; a hypothesis that follows from\nanother field is an assumption wearing a theorem's name.  Matches the\nrepair already made to the content-block sibling\n`climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.exclusionRadius_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.exclusionRadius_eq","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L576-L579","doc":"The exclusion radius is exactly `ℏ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.exclusionRadius","kind":"def","line":571,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L571-L574","doc":"The exclusion radius: `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`, derived from the categorical\nMöbius energy data. Not a free parameter — it is always `hbarQ cme.q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.energyBarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.energyBarrier","kind":"theorem","line":568,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L568-L568","doc":"**Energy barrier.**  If some pair of strand points came within the\nexclusion radius `ℏ_q`, the categorical energy would exceed every\nbound.  Stated as an implication, so an inhabitant is a configuration\nthat keeps every pair *outside* `ℏ_q` — which is the physical content\n(\"the filament cannot pass through itself\"), recovered as\n`separation_ge_exclusionRadius` below.\n\n**This field asserted the consequent unconditionally until\n2026-08-30**, as `∀ E₀ : ℝ, ∃ ε : ℝ, ε > 0 ∧ (∀ _s _t : ℝ, cme.energy\n> E₀)`.  The two `_s _t` binders were unused, so the inner `∀` was a\nconstant and the field reduced to `∀ E₀ : ℝ, cme.energy > E₀` — the\nenergy exceeds every real.  Instantiating at `E₀ := cme.energy` gives\n`cme.energy > cme.energy`, so `NonSelfIntersection M` was\n**uninhabitable for every `M`** (machine-checked: `IsEmpty\n(NonSelfIntersection M)`), and every result conditional on it was\nvacuous.  The docstring's own quantifier order (`∀ ε, ∃ E₀`) was the\nreverse of the code's, and the proximity antecedent it describes was\nnever written as a hypothesis at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.separation","kind":"def","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L549-L549","doc":"Ambient separation between the strand points at parameters `s` and `t`.\n\n`KnotEmbedding` carries only `arcLengthDist` — an *intrinsic* distance\nalong the curve — so the ambient separation that the `1/r²` kernel is a\nfunction of does not exist anywhere upstream.  It is carried here\nbecause the barrier cannot be stated without it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.cme","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.cme","kind":"def","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L542-L542","doc":"The categorical Möbius energy data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L540-L540","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.NonSelfIntersection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.NonSelfIntersection","kind":"structure","line":521,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L521-L569","doc":"**Corollary: Obstruction to self-intersection.**\n\nFor `q ≠ 1`, the non-cocommutativity of the Hopf structure provides a\ncategorical obstruction to knot self-intersection: the energy diverges\nwhenever two non-adjacent strands approach within distance `ℏ_q`.\n\nThe mechanism:\n- The universal R-matrix `R ∈ U_q(su(2)) ⊗̂ U_q(su(2))` controls the\n  failure of cocommutativity: `σ ∘ Δ ≠ Δ`.\n- The q-deformed commutator `[X̂, P̂]_q = iℏ_q` replaces the `1/r²`\n  kernel with `[2]_q / (r² − ℏ_q²)`.\n- This kernel has a hard singularity at `r = ℏ_q`, creating an energy\n  barrier of infinite height — the \"quantum exclusion zone\".\n\nPhysically, the vortex filament `γ` cannot pass through itself because\ndoing so would require infinite categorical energy. This is the\nknot-theoretic analogue of the Pauli exclusion principle.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{cor:non-self-intersection}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:non-self-intersection","label":"prf:non-self-intersection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/non-self-intersection-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qRepulsionKernel_unbounded_near_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qRepulsionKernel_unbounded_near_pole","kind":"theorem","line":488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L488-L519","doc":"**The genuine divergence.**  For `q > 1` the kernel exceeds every bound\nat radii strictly outside the exclusion radius `ℏ_q`, so it is unbounded\nas `r ↘ ℏ_q`.  This is the energy barrier the non-self-intersection\ncorollary rests on; `qRepulsionKernel_junk_value_at_pole` above is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumTwo_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumTwo_pos","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L482-L486","doc":"The quantum integer `[2]_q` is positive when `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L476-L480","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is positive when `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qRepulsionKernel_junk_value_at_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qRepulsionKernel_junk_value_at_pole","kind":"theorem","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L459-L474","doc":"At the pole itself the kernel evaluates to `0` — **Lean's `x / 0 = 0`\njunk value, not a statement about the singularity.**\n\nThis declaration was named `qRepulsionKernel_singular` and documented as\n\"the q-deformed kernel diverges at `r = ℏ_q`\" while concluding `= 0`,\nproved by `div_zero`.  The name and the docstring asserted a divergence;\nthe statement asserted its opposite, and the proof established only the\ndivision convention.  Renamed and re-documented 2026-08-30; the genuine\ndivergence is `qRepulsionKernel_unbounded_near_pole` below, and it is\nthat lemma — not this one — that the non-self-intersection corollary\nneeds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qRepulsionKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qRepulsionKernel","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L451-L457","doc":"**q-Deformed repulsion kernel**.\n\nAt `q ≠ 1`, the classical `1/r²` kernel is replaced by\n$$\\frac{[2]_q}{r^2 - \\hbarQ^2}$$\nwhich has a hard singularity at `r = ℏ_q`, creating an energy barrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusEnergy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusEnergy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L440-L447","doc":"The categorical Möbius energy is non-negative (inheriting from the\nclassical bound and the normalisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L408-L438","doc":"**Proposition: Categorical recovery of Möbius energy.**\n\nIn the classical limit `q → 1`, the categorical Möbius energy recovers\nthe classical Möbius energy up to a topological normalisation:\n$$\\lim_{q \\to 1} E_{\\mathrm{cat}}(\\gamma) = \\frac{1}{4} E(\\gamma) + \\mathrm{const}.$$\n\nThe proof proceeds in three steps:\n1. **Gauge fixing** — the categorical volume constraint fixes `G = SU(2)`,\n   ensuring `E_cat` is Möbius-invariant.\n2. **Frobenius–Hopf kernel expansion** — at `q = 1`, the comultiplication\n   becomes cocommutative and the Frobenius pairing reduces to the Killing\n   form, yielding the `1/r²` repulsive kernel.\n3. **Self-energy subtraction** — the diagonal regularisation matches the\n   arc-length subtraction via the antipode `S`.\n\nStated along the whole Möbius orbit rather than at the base energy\nalone. In that form it is **derived** from two fields — invariance\ncarries the transformed energy back to `E_cat`, and the classical\nlimit then applies — rather than returned verbatim.\n\nThe base case is `cme.classicalLimit` itself, which is what this\ndeclaration used to restate: `theorem MobiusEnergy … :=\ncme.classicalLimit`, the structure field under a second name. Use\nthe field directly when the orbit plays no part.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:mobius-energy}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:mobius-energy","label":"prf:mobius-energy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/mobius-energy-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumTwo","kind":"def","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L403-L404","doc":"The quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L400-L401","doc":"The quantum Planck constant at a given substrate parameter value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalLimit","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L398-L398","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalLimitConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalLimitConst","kind":"def","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L397-L397","doc":"**Classical limit**: as `q → 1`, the categorical energy recovers the\nclassical Möbius energy up to topological normalisation.\nEncoded as: `E_cat = (1/4) · E_classical + const`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.mobiusInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.mobiusInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L393-L393","doc":"**Möbius invariance**: `E_cat(γ)` is invariant under the full Möbius\ngroup `PSL(2, ℂ)`. Encoded as: the transformed energy equals the\nbase energy for every group element `g` — the energy functional is\nconstant along every Möbius orbit (categorical: invariance under\n`Aut⊗(ω)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.energyUnderMobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.energyUnderMobius","kind":"def","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L387-L387","doc":"The categorical energy of the knot after applying the Möbius\ntransform with parameter `g ∈ PSL(2, ℂ)` (parametrised here by a\nreal coordinate on the group, acting on the `ℂP¹` fibre via the\ngauge group fixed by the categorical volume constraint). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalEnergy","kind":"def","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L382-L382","doc":"The classical Möbius energy of the same knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.energy","kind":"def","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L380-L380","doc":"The categorical energy value `E_cat(γ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.knot","kind":"def","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L378-L378","doc":"The knot embedding in the fibre space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L376-L376","doc":"`q > 1` (non-classical regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.q","kind":"def","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L374-L374","doc":"The q-parameter value at the base point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.basepoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.basepoint","kind":"def","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L372-L372","doc":"A chosen base point for evaluating the substrate field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.sp","kind":"def","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L370-L370","doc":"The substrate parameter governing the q-deformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L368-L368","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMobiusEnergy","kind":"structure","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L355-L398","doc":"**Categorical Möbius energy data** for a knot `γ` in a quantum observable\nuniverse `(C, A, ω)`.\n\nThe energy functional is\n$$E_{\\mathrm{cat}}(\\gamma) = \\lambda \\circ \\mathrm{tr}_A\n  \\iint_{S^1 \\times S^1 \\setminus \\mathrm{diag}}\n  (\\Delta(\\gamma(s)) \\otimes \\Delta(\\gamma(t)))\n  \\star_q \\|d\\gamma/ds \\wedge_q d\\gamma/dt\\|\\,ds\\,dt$$\n\nwhere `Δ` is the Hopf comultiplication, `λ` is the Frobenius form,\nand `⋆_q` is the q-Hodge star.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:mobius-energy}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.nonempty_linkEmbedding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.nonempty_linkEmbedding","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L310-L349","doc":"**`LinkEmbedding` is inhabitable**, exhibited rather than asserted.\n\nThis file's own history is the reason to check: `NonSelfIntersection`\ncarried a field asserting `∀ E₀, energy > E₀` and was therefore\n**uninhabitable for every `M`**, which made every result conditional on it\nvacuous — sorry-free, and seen by no detector. A new structure with five\ninteracting fields earns the same scrutiny.\n\nWitness: components with all distances `0`, and a separation that is the\ncomponent's own `ambientDist` on the diagonal and `1` off it.  Degenerate on\npurpose — the point is that the field set is *consistent*, not that this is\na link anyone wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_smul","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L295-L308","doc":"**The scaling ingredient.**  Rescaling every separation by `c > 0` scales\nthe mutual integrand by `c⁻²`.\n\nThis is *not* scale-invariance of the energy — that also needs the `ds dt`\nmeasure to scale by `c²`, which requires the integral this file does not\nbuild.  It is the pointwise half, recorded so the mechanism is visible and\nthe missing half is named rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_self","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L283-L293","doc":"On one component the link-level and component-level ambient distances\nagree, so the mutual integrand restricted to `i = i` is the *unsubtracted*\npart of that component's own O'Hara integrand.\n\nThis is the statement that the two integrands are the same object seen at\ndifferent index pairs — the diagonal carries a subtraction, the off-diagonal\ndoes not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.selfIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.selfIntegrand","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L273-L281","doc":"The **self** integrand of one component is the O'Hara one, subtraction and\nall.  Recorded so the two halves of a link's energy — `Σᵢ self` and\n`Σ_{i<j} mutual` — are both expressible here.\n\nOnly the summation and integration are missing, and they need measure\ntheory this file does not set up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_symm","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L266-L271","doc":"The mutual integrand is symmetric under exchanging the two components\ntogether with their parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_pos_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand_pos_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L253-L264","doc":"**Unconditional positivity on distinct components.**\n\nThe bare-function `mutualIntegrand_pos` above needs `0 < sep s t` supplied\nas a hypothesis.  Here it is discharged from `disjoint`: nothing is assumed\nbeyond `i ≠ j`.  That is the whole reason to have this structure — a\nper-pair EM weight built this way is positive *because the carrier is a\nlink*, not because positivity was assumed of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mutualIntegrand","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L247-L251","doc":"The **mutual integrand** between component `i` at `s` and component `j` at\n`t`, stated through the link structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep_self","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L241-L241","doc":"Restricted to one component, the link-level separation is that\ncomponent's own ambient distance — so the two notions agree where they\noverlap rather than sitting side by side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L237-L237","doc":"**Distinct components never meet.**  This is what makes the configuration\na *link* rather than a singular map, and it is exactly the hypothesis that\nmakes the mutual integrand unconditionally positive below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L233-L233","doc":"Separation is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep_symm","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L231-L231","doc":"Separation is symmetric under exchanging the two (component, parameter)\npairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.sep","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L228-L228","doc":"Ambient distance from `component i` at parameter `s` to `component j` at\nparameter `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.component","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.component","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L225-L225","doc":"The components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L223-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LinkEmbedding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LinkEmbedding","kind":"structure","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L216-L241","doc":"An **`n`-component link embedding**: `n` parametrised components in `M`,\ntogether with the ambient separation between a point on any component and a\npoint on any other.\n\nThe separation is carried at link level rather than assembled from the\ncomponents, because `KnotEmbedding.ambientDist` relates two points on *the\nsame* curve and there is nothing in that structure relating two curves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mutualIntegrand_eq_ohara_without_subtraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mutualIntegrand_eq_ohara_without_subtraction","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L199-L205","doc":"The mutual integrand is the `D → ∞` limit of the O'Hara integrand, stated as\nthe algebraic identity that makes the two comparable: dropping the\nsubtracted term is exactly setting `1/D² = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mutualIntegrand_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mutualIntegrand_pos","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L184-L197","doc":"**The mutual integrand is strictly positive** wherever the two components do\nnot touch — with no hypothesis beyond that, and in particular with no\nchord-vs-arc inequality.\n\nContrast `oharaIntegrand_nonneg`, which needs `chord_le_arc` and yields only\n`0 ≤`.  The mutual term is unconditionally `0 <`, which is exactly the\nproperty bean `qou-o6ml` route (2) asks of a per-pair weight: *nonzero for\nunlinked pairs*.  On the Borromean carrier every pairwise `lk_ij = 0`\n(axiom (A3) of `mirror_split_s3_em_functional_probe.py`), so a weight built\nfrom linking numbers vanishes there while this one does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mutualIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mutualIntegrand","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L166-L182","doc":"The **mutual (cross) integrand** between points on two distinct components:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{|\\gamma_i(s) - \\gamma_j(t)|^2}.$$\n\n**No subtraction.**  The subtracted term in `oharaIntegrand` is `1/D(s,t)²`\nwith `D` the arc-length distance *along the curve*; for points on different\ncomponents there is no path along the curve at all, so `D = ∞` and the term\nvanishes identically.  The mutual energy is the unsubtracted integral, and\nthe regularisation question does not arise because distinct components are\ndisjoint — there is no diagonal to be singular on.\n\nModelled here as a bare separation function rather than through\n`KnotEmbedding`, because that structure carries a single `curve : ℝ → M` and\n**cannot express a multi-component link at all**.  That is the real gap on\nroute (2), and naming it is the point of this block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.oharaIntegrand_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.oharaIntegrand_symm","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L153-L157","doc":"The integrand is symmetric in its two parameters, inherited from the two\ndistance symmetries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.oharaIntegrand_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.oharaIntegrand_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L132-L151","doc":"**The O'Hara integrand is pointwise non-negative** off the diagonal.\n\nDerived from `chord_le_arc`, not assumed.  `ClassicalMobiusEnergy.nonneg`\nbelow is a *field* — the positivity of the energy is carried as a hypothesis\nthere because the structure has no integrand to derive it from.  This lemma\nsupplies the pointwise half of that derivation: the remaining step is that\nan integral of a non-negative function is non-negative, which needs\nintegration theory this file does not set up.\n\nThe hypothesis is that the two points are distinct in the ambient space,\nwhich is exactly the off-diagonal condition the double integral imposes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.oharaIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.oharaIntegrand","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L116-L130","doc":"The **O'Hara / Möbius integrand** at parameters `(s, t)`:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{|\\gamma(s) - \\gamma(t)|^2} - \\frac{1}{D(\\gamma(s), \\gamma(t))^2}.$$\n\nThe subtracted term is the *regularisation*: the singularity of the ambient\nterm as `t → s` is cancelled by the intrinsic term, which is what makes the\ndouble integral converge.  It is also, structurally, why this functional is\na candidate where an unsubtracted kernel is not — see bean `qou-17mq`, whose\nO2 (neutrality) obstruction excludes pair kernels that are not zero-mean; a\nkernel whose subtraction is intrinsic is not vulnerable to that argument.\n\nRef: [ohara1991], [freedman1994] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.unknot_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.unknot_iff","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The energy equals 4 if and only if the knot is the unknot\n(Freedman–He–Wang, 1994).\n\n**This field read `value = 4 ↔ True` until 2026-08-30.** `P ↔ True`\nis `P`, so that spelling forced `value = 4` for *every* instance —\nmachine-checked, `c.unknot_iff.mpr trivial : c.value = 4` — which is\nnot a weakened form of Freedman–He–Wang but the negation of its\ncontent: it made the classical Möbius energy blind to the knot, and\nthrough `CategoricalMobiusEnergy.classicalLimit` made `E_cat` blind\ntoo (`E_cat = 1 + const` for every knot).  It carried no `sorry`, no\n`axiom` and no tautological *conclusion*, so no vacuity detector saw\nit, and a prior audit (bean `qou-u87j`) cited its presence as\nevidence the library encoding was *stronger* than its content-block\nsibling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.isUnknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.isUnknot","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Whether the underlying knot is the unknot.  Carried as an opaque\n`Prop` because this structure holds no isotopy-class data; it is the\nminimum needed to *state* Freedman–He–Wang rather than assert its\nconclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The energy is non-negative (Freedman–He–Wang). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.value","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The energy value `E(γ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ClassicalMobiusEnergy","kind":"structure","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L80-L114","doc":"The **classical Möbius energy** of a knot embedding.\n\n$$E(\\gamma) = \\iint_{S^1 \\times S^1}\n  \\left(\\frac{1}{|\\gamma(s) - \\gamma(t)|^2}\n    - \\frac{1}{D(\\gamma(s), \\gamma(t))^2}\\right)\n  |\\gamma'(s)|\\,|\\gamma'(t)|\\,ds\\,dt.$$\n\nRef: [freedman1994], [ohara1991]\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:mobius-energy}` (classical part) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.chord_le_arc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.chord_le_arc","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L78-L78","doc":"**The chord never exceeds the arc.**  This is what makes the O'Hara\nintegrand pointwise non-negative, and hence what makes\n`ClassicalMobiusEnergy.nonneg` a consequence rather than an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.ambient_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.ambient_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Ambient distance is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.ambient_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.ambient_symm","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Ambient distance is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.ambientDist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.ambientDist","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L70-L70","doc":"**Ambient (chord) distance** `|γ(s) − γ(t)|` between the strand points at\nparameters `s` and `t`.\n\nCarried as a field rather than obtained from a `MetricSpace M` instance,\nmatching how `arcLengthDist` is already carried: `M` is the fibre of the\nrealisation functor and the rest of this file keeps it a bare `Type*`, so\nrequiring a metric instance would constrain every use site for one\ndefinition.\n\nAdded 2026-08-30 (bean `qou-o6ml`, route 2). Until then this structure\ncarried only the *intrinsic* distance, so the Möbius/O'Hara integrand —\nwhich is a function of the **ambient** separation minus the intrinsic one\n— could not be written in this encoding at all, and the `ClassicalMobiusEnergy`\ndocstring stated an integral none of the data here could express. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.arcLength_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.arcLength_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Arc-length distance is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.arcLength_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.arcLength_symm","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Arc-length distance is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.arcLengthDist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.arcLengthDist","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Arc-length distance along the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.curve","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The parametrised curve `γ : [0, 1] → M` (periodic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotEmbedding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotEmbedding","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusEnergy.lean#L42-L78","doc":"A **knot embedding** `γ : S¹ → M` in the fibre of the realisation functor,\nequipped with smooth parametrisation data.\n\nIn the categorical setting, `γ` takes values in `ω(A)` where `ω` is the\nfibre functor and `A` is the Frobenius–Hopf object. ","signatureChunk":0}]}